                "text": "Protect My Prayer is a feature in the Lunora app. When a prayer time comes in, the apps you have chosen wait for a short time, 15 minutes by default. When you tap “I prayed” in Lunora they open right away, and the prayer is marked in your prayer log."
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How long do the apps stay locked?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "15 minutes by default, counted from the start of the prayer time. On Android you can choose 10, 15 or 20 minutes, and on iPhone 15 or 20. If you tap “I prayed” they open immediately; if you don't, they open on their own when the time is up."
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Can I open an app in an emergency?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes. Tap “An emergency? Lift it now” and the apps open straight away; they are protected again at the next prayer. The Phone app and Lunora are never made to wait."
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Does Protect My Prayer work on iPhone?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes. On iPhone it uses Apple's Screen Time permission and needs iOS 16 or later. On Android it uses Usage access and the permission to display over other apps."
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What happens during my period?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Protect My Prayer rests on its own while Period Mode is on and comes back when your period ends. It doesn't ask you, your chosen apps and prayers are kept, and period days don't break your prayer streak."
